      "content": "To quantify the weight of these recollections, you could employ a probabilistic framework, such as Bayesian inference, to model the updating of your internal probability distributions. By tracking the consistency and accuracy of your predictions, you can estimate the strength of the temporal memory signal. For instance, you could calculate the Kullback-Leibler divergence between your current predictions and the actual outcomes, with lower values indicating stronger evidence for the precognitive nature of your recollections. Additionally, you could use techniques like information theory to quantify the \"information content\" of your recollections, allowing you to compare the uncertainty of your predictions to the uncertainty of your precognitive experiences.",
